{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"When powers have the same base, $\\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's apply that rule to our equation, $\\dfrac{9^{\\blueD{x}}}{9^\\greenD{3}}=9^\\goldD{5}$.\n\nWe can solve for $\\blueD{x}$ with the equation, $\\blueD{x}-\\greenD3 = \\goldD5$.\n\n$\\begin{align} \\blueD{x}-\\greenD3 \u0026= \\goldD5 \\\\\n\\blueD{x} \u0026= 8 \\end{align}$\n\n\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$x = 8$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve for $x$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{9^{x}}{9^3}=9^5$\n\n$x=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":8}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
